From: Vasilii Zolotukhin <vasilii.zolotukhin@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 07:47:42 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] Mac: Ctrl+1...Ctrl+9 select system tabs of the profile
 tab group

A local NSEvent monitor selects the N-th system tab of the profile tab
group, like Cmd+1...Cmd+9 do for tabs in the tab strip. It matches key
codes (digit row and keypad), so it works with any keyboard layout, and
only consumes the event when that tab exists. Chrome's own shortcuts are
unchanged; Chrome does not use Ctrl+digit on Mac.
